@page "/legal/withdrawal"

<PageTitle>Right of Withdrawal</PageTitle>

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-9 col-xl-8">

        <h1 class="mb-3">Right of Withdrawal and Refunds</h1>
        <p class="text-body-secondary fst-italic mb-4">Last updated: [Date]</p>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">1. Who You Buy From</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                LetterLoom is sold through <strong>Paddle.com Market Ltd</strong> (“Paddle”) as Merchant of Record.
                Paddle is the legal seller for consumer-law purposes. The purchase contract is concluded between you
                and Paddle. Paddle’s
                <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/buyer-terms" class="link-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    Buyer Terms
                </a>
                and Paddle’s refund policy apply to the transaction.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">2. Statutory Right of Withdrawal (Consumers)</h2>
            <p>
                As a consumer in the EU/EEA, you generally have a <strong>14-day right of withdrawal</strong>
                from the date of contract conclusion. To exercise this right, you must inform Paddle (as the seller)
                or us by means of a clear statement (e.g. email) of your decision to withdraw.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Contact for withdrawal requests:
                <span>stephan.emmermann[at]gmail.com</span>
                or Paddle’s buyer support at
                <a href="https://paddle.net" class="link-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">paddle.net</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">3. Early Expiry for Digital Content</h2>
            <p>
                LetterLoom is digital content supplied immediately.
                <strong>
                    The right of withdrawal expires
                    once performance has begun
                </strong> - in particular when the license key is activated or the
                software is downloaded and made available to you - provided that:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>you have given your express consent to immediate performance during checkout, and</li>
                <li>you have confirmed your awareness that you thereby lose your right of withdrawal.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-0">
                At checkout, Paddle will obtain the required consent and confirmation. If you do not provide the
                consent, performance will not begin immediately and the statutory withdrawal right continues to apply.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">4. Consequences of Withdrawal</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                If a valid withdrawal is exercised, Paddle will reimburse the payments received without undue delay
                and at the latest within 14 days of receiving the withdrawal notice, using the same payment method
                unless otherwise agreed. If performance has already begun and the statutory requirements for early
                expiry are not met, statutory rules on partial performance apply.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">5. Refunds and Defective Products</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Paddle’s refund policy applies to the transaction. Your statutory rights for defective digital
                products (e.g. if the software is not as described, is faulty, or is not fit for purpose) remain
                unaffected and take precedence over any discretionary refund policy.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">6. B2B Customers</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The statutory right of withdrawal applies only to consumers. Business customers do not have a
                statutory withdrawal right. Refunds for business customers are at the discretion of Paddle under
                its Buyer Terms.
            </p>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>